    "name": "Red Currant Berries",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Red currants are&nbsp;small, tart, red berries native to parts of Western Europe, belonging to the Ribes genus.&nbsp;They are known for their bright red color, translucent flesh, and a flavor that is both sweet and tart with citrusy notes.&nbsp;Red currants are rich in vitamins C and K, antioxidants, and are relatively low in calories.&nbsp;They are commonly used in jams, jellies, pies, juices, and even wines.&nbsp;</span></p>",
